// kite::alloc::collections — aggregator for the PUBLIC collection modules. `import kite::alloc::collections`
// brings the whole target-tier collections family into scope by short name (Vec, Array, Deque, HashMap,
// HashSet, TreeMap, TreeSet) without needing a per-type import line.
//
// It re-exports only the PUBLIC types. It does NOT re-export the `internal::*` modules (intbuf/rawmap/rawbuf):
// those are language primitives auto-injected via the prelude (they back the `[..]`/`{..}` literals) and are
// not part of the public collections surface — a program should reach for Vec/HashMap, not IntBuf/RawMap.
// Vec/Array/HashMap are ALSO prelude modules, so a program gets them even without this aggregator; the
// module collector dedups imports by path (the prelude paths seed `seen`), so re-exporting them here adds no
// duplicate definition. Deque/HashSet/TreeMap/TreeSet are NOT in the prelude, so this aggregator is the
// convenient single opt-in that makes them reachable by short name. (The packed sized-byte arrays
// kite::alloc::collections::bytes stay a separate opt-in, re-exported by kite::alloc, not here.)
pub import kite::alloc::collections::vec
pub import kite::alloc::collections::array
pub import kite::alloc::collections::deque
pub import kite::alloc::collections::hashmap
pub import kite::alloc::collections::hashset
pub import kite::alloc::collections::treemap
pub import kite::alloc::collections::treeset
